  "rationale": "Austin, San Diego, and Seattle are the study markets. Each is one metro (latitude standard deviation about 0.05\u20130.07, not an archipelago), the Inside Airbnb snapshot is from 2025, and bedrooms are almost complete. Austin has 10,323 listings inside the $25\u2013$2,000 window and only 16 missing prices. San Diego has 11,613 and Seattle 6,004; Seattle has almost no listings above the $2,000 cap, so the tail does not dominate. Hawaii is many islands in one file. Las Vegas, Fort Lauderdale, and Nashville are missing a nightly price on roughly 30% of rows. Asheville's bedrooms column is essentially empty. The other snapshots stay on disk and are not in the headline results.",
